parent). Written as the case ran. **Case 3 of 4 in group A.**

## 🔴 THE AUTHORED PROCEDURE WAS NOT FOLLOWED. Read this first.

This case is the only one in the campaign with authored steps, and **they could not be run on
this bench.** Stating that plainly is a requirement of the Test Engineer's approval, not a
footnote.

**What the case authors wrote.** `AWPTCM-T9032`, `src=xml` (the legacy corpus), status
**Approved**, folder `/Interop/Windows_IO/802.1x`. Its 15 steps are a **person driving Internet
Explorer's certificate import wizard on a Windows PC**, verbatim:

> Prepare Route and the Supplicant certificate before the test. … They are copied onto
> Supplicant. Start the Internet Explorer on Supplicant. 1) Click Tool button. 2) Click Internet
> option. 3) Click Contents tab. 4) Click Certificate button. ■ Certificate screen 5) Click
> Import button. … 13) Click Finish button. 14) Check that the certificate was added. 15) The
> route certificate is similarly added.  Should be success. See and check the packet sequence.
> When PC and switch are connected, certificate tab is opened. Packet sequence is correct.

and the precondition names the environment outright: `Environment: Windows PC`.

**Why they were not followed.** **There is no Windows PC on tb277, and no GUI of any kind.** The
bench is a Linux testbox driving serial consoles. Steps 1–15 are mouse clicks in a browser that
does not exist here. No amount of bench work makes them runnable; they are not blocked by a
missing cable or a licence.

**What was done instead, and on whose authority.** The Test Engineer decided on 2026-10-23 to
**redesign the case with `wpa_supplicant` on tb277**, grading on the packet exchange rather than
on a GUI. A **step-level MANUAL-ONLY row already exists** for the certificate-import limb. The
authored **objective** is what this run measures, and it is quoted here in full because it is the
thing being graded:

> **"Confirm that an authenticator exchanges authentication messages between the supplicant and
> Radius server."**

The authored **precondition** was used as written wherever this build still accepts it — it is
the source of the local-RADIUS recipe the whole group runs on — and every place this build
differs from it is recorded below.

**Nothing in this log should be read as a claim that the authored steps were executed.**

